Forward CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE into the SPIRV translator sub-build.

The ExternalProject forwards compilers and LLVM_DIR but not the build
type, so the sub-build configures with an EMPTY build type; with
single-config Ninja its `--config Release` is ignored and on MSVC the
translator links against a different runtime than LLVM
(_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL mismatch). Fixed upstream on develop
(CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE now forwarded via CMAKE_ARGS), so this is a
release-pin backport only.

diff --git a/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt b/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -207,2 +207,3 @@
       CMAKE_CACHE_ARGS
+        -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE:STRING=${CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE}
         -DLLVM_SPIRV_BUILD_EXTERNAL:BOOL=YES
